{"id": "EUVD-2026-86860", "enisaUuid": "05b34d39-bcd2-3ffd-85a4-1fb239cc55c0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: initialise error in xfs_defer_finish_one()\n\nxfs_defer_finish_one() declares error without an initialiser and only\nassigns it inside the loop over dfp->dfp_work.  When that list is empty\nthe loop body never runs, control falls through to the \"Done with the\ndfp, free it\" path, and the function returns an indeterminate value.\n\nAn item-less pending item reaches this through xfs_defer_add_barrier(),\nwhich xfs_reap_ag_blocks() uses on any CONFIG_XFS_ONLINE_REPAIR kernel.\nxfs_defer_finish_noroll() treats any non-EAGAIN return as fatal, so a\nnon-zero stack value turns a successful barrier into a\nSHUTDOWN_CORRUPT_INCORE in the middle of a repair.  Zero is the correct\nresult: reaching the free path means the item loop drained without a\nnon-zero error.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30748a24b9f04f9a83599ba907cc8fbff0729f3c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba949a14446b7346e92e676ee3fe2bb79d9ce450", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b507c239884f7d4bf8339f6e9eb8bfcb540afde", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6176d21d7bd609632c5b7e87a3adb9be29ec1e72"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97552", "GHSA-8vjw-786p-wjm9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4f05af74-1061-3c5c-9e34-d376999ad4aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f3cec031099c37513727efc978a12b6346e326d <ba949a14446b7346e92e676ee3fe2bb79d9ce450"}, {"id": "579a9aad-7d97-3527-944a-4e60df9d31e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f3cec031099c37513727efc978a12b6346e326d <6176d21d7bd609632c5b7e87a3adb9be29ec1e72"}, {"id": "6518fb00-9359-37f4-ae4b-e76347158f59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "8df9d91f-3488-3e61-81d3-d0e1219432e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "99188843-1401-38c8-8efb-6d578df50086", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f3cec031099c37513727efc978a12b6346e326d <30748a24b9f04f9a83599ba907cc8fbff0729f3c"}, {"id": "b09269f8-dd6d-34ed-9853-12493655702a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d7e6c02e-cabe-3954-8f69-19261c0f110b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "e2a72a16-2dc9-385b-8d4a-d881add39771", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "faab233e-0335-3289-81b1-19cfce60dd16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f3cec031099c37513727efc978a12b6346e326d <6b507c239884f7d4bf8339f6e9eb8bfcb540afde"}, {"id": "fe4b2ecc-eafc-3db0-8171-e7629fb16986", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b0117da2-92e7-3169-a9dd-0324e100c406", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}